{% /aside %}

## Where the survey took place

Mt. Tujuh is a volcano in the Barisan Mountains of western Sumatra, inside
Kerinci Seblat National Park. Close to its summit (2,732 m) is Lake Gunung Tujuh, 
a crater lake about 4.5 km long and 3 km wide at roughly 2,000 m above sea level.

![Map of Sumatra, the southern Malay Peninsula, and western Java with a marker on Mt. Tujuh in Kerinci, Jambi, in the southern half of Sumatra near its west coast, and Jakarta marked for reference](../../../../../assets/images/tutorials/basic/mt-tujuh-map.svg)

Picture the camp from the water. The team stayed at Pondok Merah, on the edge of
the lake at 2,004 m. From a boat, the camp is a blue tarp against a wall of
montane forest:

![A blue tarp camp on the lake shore, seen from a boat, below steep montane forest](../../../../../assets/images/tutorials/basic/tujuh-camp-far.webp)

Closer in, the shore is a narrow strip of grass between the water and the trees.
The trap lines ran into the forest on both sides of camp.

![The camp closer up from the lake: a blue tarp and an orange tent on a strip of grass at the forest edge](../../../../../assets/images/tutorials/basic/tujuh-camp-near.webp)

![The camp from the lake on a brighter day, with tall trees behind the tarp and choppy green water in front](../../../../../assets/images/tutorials/basic/tujuh-camp-shore.webp)

Under the tarp, the camp was also the lab. The team prepared specimens on a
field table here, and young Heru wrote the journal here.

![Under the camp tarp: a field table on a log frame with tools, paper towels, and supplies, and water containers on the ground](../../../../../assets/images/tutorials/basic/tujuh-camp-tarp.webp)

Pasir Putih, the second survey area, lies across the lake. Reaching it took a
1.5-hour ride by wooden boat. The team ran those lines on day trips from camp.
Keep this layout in mind—one camp, two areas, and a lake between them. It
explains most of the locality problems in the paper catalog.

## Series overview

| Tutorial | What you enter | Core NAHPU concept |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [1. Meet the paper catalog](/en/tutorials/basic/paper-catalog/) | Nothing yet | Read the source critically and spot its problems |
| [2. Create the project](/en/tutorials/basic/project-personnel-taxa/) | Project, personnel, and taxa | Enter shared context once |
| [3. Create sites](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/) | One camp and six trap/pitfall lines | One place, one reusable record |
| [4. Record collecting events](/en/tutorials/basic/events/) | When, how, and by whom each line was run | The bridge between place and specimen |
| [5. Enter specimen records](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/) | Seven representative specimens | Linked, validated fields |
| [6. Correct and enter the journal](/en/tutorials/basic/narrative/) | Five corrected journal entries | Field context that has no form field |
| [7. Review records and statistics](/en/tutorials/basic/review-records/) | Nothing new; a final check | Review the dataset as a whole |
