Allow about two hours for the full series. You can follow along on a tablet or
computer; a phone works, but a larger screen makes it easier to learn.

## What the paper catalog looks like

Each printed sheet holds four specimens under a single `Locality` header. Below
is the top of the first sheet, showing the locality followed by HH 436 and
HH 437:

![Paper specimen form with the locality header for Mt. Tujuh, Sungai Jernih, Pondok Merah, and the records for HH 436, Lariscus insignis, and HH 437, Mus crociduroides](../../../../../assets/images/tutorials/basic/paper-hh436-437.jpg)

The form provides a structured way to record the following information: collector number, species, standard
measurements, sex and reproductive condition, capture date and time, method,
trap line, tissues, habitat, and remarks. The trouble is not the fields
themselves, but how the values relate to one another across sheets and
notebooks.

## Problems in Heru's paper records

The table below lists the issues found across the full specimen catalog and
journal; the two crops on this page illustrate several of them. Each issue comes
back later in the tutorial where NAHPU solves it.

| Problem on paper | Example | How NAHPU handles it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Locality written once per sheet; later sheets left blank | Every sheet after the first, including specimens from Pasir Putih across the lake | Specimens link to an event, and the event links to its site ([Tutorials 3–5](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/)) |
| Elevation unit crossed out and inconsistent | `Elev. 2004 feet m.` on sheet 1; `2004 m asl` on sheet 2 | Elevation is always stored in meters ([Tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/)) |
| Hemisphere letters with no datum or uncertainty | `01.70274° S 101.39032° E` | Signed decimal degrees, explicit datum, and uncertainty fields ([Tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/)) |
| Multiple spellings for one species | `Maxorys`, `Maxomy`, `Maxotys`, `hylomyoider`, `hylomyoides` | Pick every name from one taxon registry ([Tutorial 2](/en/tutorials/basic/project-personnel-taxa/)) |
| Corrections written over original values | HH 437: number written over `436`; `male` scribbled out for `female` | Fields hold one clean value chosen from a list ([Tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/)) |
| Struck-out identification with no determiner or date | HH 456: `Mus crociduroides` crossed out for `Maxomys hylomyoides` | Dedicated `Determiner`, `ID Confidence`, and `Remarks` fields ([Tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/)) |
| Out-of-sequence date and missing fields | HH 442 reads `17 Sept` among 13 September records, with no time, line, or age | Records are reviewed in context and explained in remarks ([Tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/)) |
| Standard capture time with no explanation | Most forms read `07.00`—the team's convention for overnight captures—but nothing on the form states this | Documented once in each event's notes ([Tutorial 4](/en/tutorials/basic/events/)) |
| `Line 1` names two methods | Pitfalls and snap traps were both labeled Line 1 | Separate sites and events per method ([Tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/)) |
| Collector always listed as Heru | On 17 September, teammates checked Pasir Putih while Heru stayed in camp | Capture `Collector` is chosen from the event's personnel ([Tutorial 4](/en/tutorials/basic/events/)) |
| Habitat written once, on a single specimen | HH 436: `Mature secondary forest` | Habitat belongs to the site, not one animal ([Tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/)) |
| Tissue numbers and tube notes written in the `Museum` box | Tissue numbers (`Z26230`–`Z26317`) and HH 529's `Blank Tube` written in the `Museum` box, even though museums usually assign catalog numbers only after accessioning | Leave `Museum ID` empty in the field; store tissue numbers in `Tissue ID` and tube notes in part `Remarks` ([Tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/)) |
| Preparation codes with no legend | `SA` and `AL` | Explicit specimen parts with type and treatment ([Tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/)) |
| Tissue circled inconsistently | HH 442 has no tissue circled | A tissue part is added only when it exists ([Tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/)) |
| Remark that only makes sense alongside the journal | HH 523: `Underpart darker than M. hylomyoides` | Journal and specimens live in one project, linked by date and site ([Tutorial 6](/en/tutorials/basic/narrative/)) |

HH 523 is a clear example of how paper separates linked facts. Its sheet has no
locality header at all, making it look as if it came from Pondok Merah:

![Paper specimen form for HH 523, Maxomys cf. hylomyoides, from trap line 3, with the remark: underpart darker than M. hylomyoides](../../../../../assets/images/tutorials/basic/paper-hh523.jpg)

Only the field journal for 16–18 September reveals that Line 3 was at Pasir
Putih, a 1.5-hour boat ride across the lake.

## The seven records you will enter

The full catalog holds over 100 specimens. These tutorials use seven that span
both survey areas, three methods, and most of the problems above. Whenever the
paper contradicts itself, the tutorials explain which value is best supported
and why.

| Field ID | Paper spelling | Name to enter | Line | Why it was chosen |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| HH 436 | `Lariscur insignis` | *Lariscus insignis* | 1, snap trap | First record; only one with habitat; matches the 12 September journal |
| HH 437 | `Mur crociduroider` | *Mus crociduroides* | 1, snap trap | Overwritten field number and sex |
| HH 442 | `Maxomy hylomyoider` | *Maxomys hylomyoides* | Not recorded | Conflicting date; missing line, time, and age |
| HH 453 | `Crocidura beccari` | *Crocidura beccarii* | 1, pitfall | Pitfall capture sharing a line name with snap traps |
| HH 456 | `Mus crociduroides`, crossed out for `Maxotys hylomyoides` | *Maxomys hylomyoides* | 2, snap trap | Changed identification |
| HH 523 | `Maxomys cf. hylomyoider` | *Maxomys* (remark: `cf. hylomyoides`) | 3, snap trap | Pasir Putih site; remark tied to the journal; non-standard capture time |
| HH 529 | `Crocidura neglecta` | *Crocidura neglecta* | 4, pitfall | Heru listed as collector while in camp; `Blank Tube` in the museum box |

Measurements, dates, and other values follow the paper exactly unless a tutorial
notes a correction.

By the end of [Basic tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/), the seven
records appear like this in NAHPU's Data table:

![NAHPU Data table on an iPad listing the seven specimen records with cataloger, field number, family, genus, specific epithet, and sex](../../../../../assets/images/app-screenshots/tutorials/basic/data-table-specimens.webp)

